DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       ppggmmmmeeddiiaann applies a median filter to a PGM image, using either the his‐
       togram sort or select kth value method to determine the median.

       A  median  filter is a convolution filter in which the value of a pixel
       in the output is the median of a certain set of pixels in the neighbor‐
       hood  of the corresponding input pixel.  The effect is to eliminate lo‐
       cally extreme values.  Such pixels typically show up as speckles.

       Pixels at the edges of the image, pixels where the  convolution  kernel
       would  go  off the edge of the image, are just copied.  For example, if
       --hheeiigghhtt is 9, the first 4 and last 4 rows of the input image  are  just
       copied to the output.


       See  the  --ttyyppee  and  --ccuuttooffff  options for information on how ppggmmmmeeddiiaann
       chooses between the two methods.



